    "schema_version": 1,
    "seq": 5,
    "meta": {},
    "summary": "Scaffold a minimal Vite + vanilla-JS app showing \"BP03 contract\" and start the Vite dev server on port 8000.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "title": "Initialize Vite project with vanilla-JS template",
        "detail": "Run `npm create vite@latest . -- --template vanilla` to scaffold the project in the workspace root, then `npm install` to install dependencies."
      },
      {
        "title": "Set up the page content",
        "detail": "Edit main.js to render an h1 with the text 'BP03 contract' into the DOM, and ensure index.html has the right structure."
      },
      {
        "title": "Start Vite dev server on port 8000",
        "detail": "Run `npx vite --port 8000 --host` so the live preview on port 8000 serves the Vite dev server (not a static build)."
      }
    ],
    "revision": 1,
    "context": "## What I found\n- The workspace is completely empty \u2014 no existing files or config.\n\n## Approach\n- Use Vite's official `vanilla` template for the simplest possible setup (no framework, just plain JS + HTML).\n- Replace the default \"Vite + JavaScript\" heading with \"BP03 contract\".\n- Start the Vite dev server on port 8000 so the user preview is the live dev server with HMR, not a static build.\n\n## Trade-offs\n- This is intentionally minimal: no CSS framework, no build output step. The dev server IS the preview."
  },
